<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chen Youliang</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1320–1363</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chen Youliang was a Chinese rebel leader of the late Yuan period, the son of a fisherman, who rose as an officer in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xu-shouhui">Xu Shouhui</a>'s Red Turban regime on the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangtze-river">Yangtze</a>. In 1360 he killed Xu and proclaimed himself emperor of Han, the state known as Chen Han. His great fleet was destroyed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hongwu-emperor">Zhu Yuanzhang</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-poyang">Lake Poyang</a> in 1363, where Chen was killed, opening the way for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming dynasty</a>.</p></div>
